"to": 127,
"text": "The diff is OS-sensitive: the new check re-executes its own binary (a process) and gates its recording test on `cfg(unix)`. So the plan carries the operator's hygiene, push and CI-read entries: CI's «Test (windows)» and «Test (macos)» legs witness the re-executed child on each OS, and «Test (windows)» the unix-gated test's absence there. The stand-repeat and coverage legs are not local entries: CI's «Stand checks repeated» (the new `stand_` file, three rounds) and «Coverage report» (the floors: dioxus-native-dom 83 %, blitz-test-harness 90 %, keeps arch S5 and security S1) run them, and the operator's CI read asserts `verdict: green`. No dependency is added, so the audit leg is no entry: the `Cargo.lock` probe below asserts the lock does not move."
}
],
